Creator here! I built FLUX out of curiosity.
The idea: AI agents often send repetitive JSON, and a compact binary
encoding with string deduplication can shrink those payloads. It is not
automatically cheaper or faster than JSON — small messages can even be
larger, and this Python codec encodes more slowly than json.dumps.

Installation: clone https://github.com/ZodiacDog/FLUX and
`pip install -e .`

Measured numbers (not marketing estimates) are in README.md.

